# The PRINTER setting, set to LASERJET in the setup menu as a user does it,
# sends a job with no escape code at all to the HP LaserJet II: plain text
# (the desktop test's PRINT.TXT, twice, sent by PRFILES) printed in its
# Courier 10 pitch, one page at 300 dpi. Its pixels must be the ones
# tools/printer/render --laserjet draws, and its PDF the one it writes
# (make_bench_disks.sh's plain-laserjet.pages and plain-laserjet.pdf).
@disk-a tools/dev/builds/disks/plain.st
text "Atari +: (ST|STE|Mega STE), TOS" 1500
type put_str PRINTER LASERJET
key 0x1c
type save
key 0x1c
key s
key 0x1c
type print
key 0x1c
text "PRINTER .STR.: LASERJET" 300
key m
key 0x1c
text "Atari +: (ST|STE|Mega STE), TOS" 300
key f
key 0x1c
wait 100
key 0x01
wait 900
key 0x39
log "pages: job 00000001 page 1 2480x3507 MD5 cab65f82a7244f93296370d3a0d3317e" 3000
log "pages: job 00000001 rendered, 1 pages, PDF 48804 bytes, [0-9]+ us, longest pass [0-9]+ us, 0 dots lost" 1200
log "pages: job 00000001: LaserJet, [0-9]+ passes over its pages" 60
cardsame PRINTER/00000001.pdf tools/dev/builds/disks/plain-laserjet.pdf
